    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `triage` in `app/worker.py`. It's the async version of `ask_with_limits`: it makes one request per ticket and reads the answer and the token budget from that same response.\n\n```python\nasync def triage(client: AsyncAnthropic, ticket: str) -> dict:\n    raw = await client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n        model=MODEL, max_tokens=512, system=SYSTEM,\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": ticket}],\n    )\n    message = await raw.parse()\n    tokens_remaining = int(raw.headers[TOKENS_REMAINING])\n    return {\n        \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n        \"tokens_remaining\": tokens_remaining,\n        \"request_id\": raw.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n        \"throttle\": tokens_remaining < LOW_WATERMARK,\n    }\n```\n\nThe async code can't simply copy the sync version. In the pinned `anthropic` 1.x, `raw.parse()` has to be awaited on the async client, as well as the `with_raw_response.create(...)` call itself. Without the second `await`, you get a coroutine back instead of a `Message`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `pytest -q`: 2 passed. Neither existing test calls `triage`.\n- I also ran `triage` against a fake HTTP layer (no network). It sent exactly one request with the right model, `max_tokens=512`, system prompt and user message. It returned `{'answer': 'billing: refund', 'tokens_remaining': 1500, 'request_id': 'req_1', 'throttle': True}`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** the check script `_chk_triage.py` is still in the project root. Deleting it needed your approval, which wasn't granted, so please delete it or let me.\n\nI didn't add a test for `triage`. The fake-response check could go into `tests/` as one if you want."
